.TH "XmTabBoxGetNumRows" "library call"
.SH "NAME"
\fBXmTabBoxGetNumRows\fP \(em A TabBox function that returns the number of rows of tabs
.iX "XmTabBoxGetNumRows"
.iX "TabBox functions" "XmTabBoxGetNumRows"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/TabBox\&.h>
\fBint \fBXmTabBoxGetNumRows\fP\fR(
\fBWidget \fBwidget\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBXmTabBoxGetNumRows\fP returns the number of rows in which the TabBox
currently lays out its tabs\&. Only the stacked tab modes
(\fBXmTABS_STACKED\fP and \fBXmTABS_STACKED_STATIC\fP) use more
than one row; the other modes lay the tabs out in one row\&.
The value reflects the current layout of the TabBox\&.
.IP "\fIwidget\fP" 10
Specifies the TabBox widget ID\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
Returns the number of rows, or 0 if \fIwidget\fP is not a TabBox
or has no tabs\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fBXmTabBoxGetTabRow\fP(3), \fBXmTabStack\fP(3) and \fBXmTabbedStackList\fP(3)\&.
